            <div xml:id="d525">

                <pb facs="0814" n="724" sameAs="frus:frus1932v02/pg724"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.01 Foreign Control/243: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul at Geneva
                        (Gilbert)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-05-08T21:00:00-04:00">May 8, 1932—9 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>78. For Reber. The substance of Department’s telegram No. 77, May 8, 1 p.m., has
                    been communicated to Harvey Firestone, Junior. He stated that our opinion as to
                    the requirements precedent to serious discussion by them of any proposal
                    involving either a modification <pb facs="0815" n="725" xml:id="pg725"/> of the
                    loan contract or further advances represented in his view a “conservative
                    estimate”.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
